# How to compile example files

See @Taskfile for all commands, e.g.:

```bash
task example:basic
```

or

```bash
task example:shape-guard
```

Run example compilations with tracing enabled:

### Example files that can be compiled

examples/in/rfc/guard/shape_guard.ft
examples/in/rfc/guard/basic_guard.ft
examples/in/basic.ft
examples/in/go_builtins.ft
examples/in/generics.ft
examples/in/slices.ft (`task example:slices` — subslice expressions)
examples/in/string_slice.ft (`task example:string-slice` — string subslice)
examples/in/void_early_return.ft (`task example:void-early-return` — bare return in void fn)
examples/in/shape_value_mutate.ft (`task example:shape-value-mutate` — value-shape field assign+return)
examples/in/blank_ident.ft (`task example:blank-ident` — blank identifier)
examples/in/func_multi_return.ft (`task example:func-multi-return` — `: (T, error)` returns)
examples/in/method_chain.ft (`task example:method-chain` — Forst method chaining `q.Inc().Value()`)
examples/in/field_after_call.ft (`task example:field-after-call` — field on call result `makeQ().n`)
examples/in/string_quote_escape.ft (`task example:string-quote-escape` — escaped `"` in string literal)
examples/in/index_then_field.ft (`task example:index-then-field` — `xs[0].name`)
examples/in/bytes_alias.ft (`task example:bytes-alias` — `type Bytes = []Byte` → `[]byte`)
examples/in/method_multireturn/ (`task example:method-multireturn` — unpack Go method multi-return; `helpers.go` + `main.ft`)
examples/in/go_interop/cli.ft (`task example:go-interop` — Go FFI spread, field access, same-package hand-written Go)
examples/in/basic_function.ft
examples/in/ensure.ft
examples/in/ensure_bool.ft (`task example:ensure-bool` — bare `ensure b` / `ensure !b`)
examples/in/ensure_else_method.ft (`task example:ensure-else-method` — else method call + concat-in-shape)
examples/in/nominal_error.ft (`task example:nominal-error` — nominal `error X { … }` type)
examples/in/union_error_types.ft (`task example:union-error-types` — typedef `ParseError | IoError`, golden `examples/out/union_error_types.go`)
examples/in/result_ensure.ft (`task example:result-ensure` — Result + `ensure … is Ok()`)
examples/in/result_void_ensure.ft (`task example:result-void-ensure` — void+ensure → `Result(Void, Error)`)
examples/in/result_unwrap_propagate.ft (`task example:result-unwrap-propagate` — bare `ensure x is Ok()` propagates error slot)
examples/in/result_if.ft (`task example:result-if` — Result + `if x is Ok()`)
examples/in/mutual_recursion.ft (`task example:mutual-recursion` — annotated mutual method recursion)
examples/in/slice_alias_methods.ft (`task example:slice-alias-methods` — named slice alias + append)
examples/in/tictactoe/ (merged package: `task example:tictactoe`; TypeScript from `forst generate`: `task example:tictactoe:generate` — writes gitignored `examples/in/tictactoe/generated/` and `examples/in/tictactoe/client/`)

There should be corresponding outputs in the same paths just with `in` replaced by `out` (Go goldens). Tictactoe TS artifacts are not committed; regenerate locally after changing `.ft` files.

TypeScript from `forst generate`: examples registered in `examples/in/forst-generate-ts-examples.json` are covered by `TestGenerate_exampleManifest` (merged generate + optional substring checks). `tsc --noEmit` with stubs lives in `generate_tsc_test.go`. Set `FORST_SKIP_TS_E2E=1` to skip when no `tsc` is available.

## Project Structure

The project follows this structure:

- `cmd/forst/`: Main compiler executable
- `internal/`: Core packages
  - `typechecker/`: Type checking implementation
  - `parser/`: Parser implementation
  - `ast/`: Abstract Syntax Tree definitions
- `examples/in/`: Example Forst source files
  - `rfc/guard/`: Guard-related examples
  - `basic.ft`: Basic language examples
  - `generics.ft`: Built-in parameterized types (`[]T`, `*T`, `append`/`copy`/`cap`/`range`); not user-defined generics
  - `basic_function.ft`: Function examples
  - `ensure.ft`: Ensure statement examples
- `examples/out/`: Example expected Go files after transpilation

See [examples/README.md](../../examples/README.md) for how `examples/in/rfc/` mixes RFC-style docs with sample sources.
